Subject: [PATCH 01276/11171] [conductor] DECENTRALIZATION on a TRACTABLE MoE
 base -- BUILD+LAUNCH (G3; split-long-codex BUILD half; clean replacement for
 the flagged exp4022 + the 0-task exp4037): exp4012 = gemma-4-12B best-of-N
 k=8 = 0.2581 coverage (no lift). exp4037 launched 31B DENSE but scored 0
 tasks (too slow). THIS uses Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (MoE, ~3B ACTIVE -- the
 throughput fix) on the SAME 30-task ARC-1 pool as exp4012 (apples-to-apples),
 k=8, BATCHED generation + RoBoN-style early-stop (arXiv:2512.05542), same
 model-free demo-fit verifier. Per 'The Invisible Leash' (arXiv:2507.14843) +
 RL-vs-Distillation (arXiv:2505.14216): a stronger base raises the CEILING
 only if the ARC-induction abstraction is LATENT in it. Smoke on 2 tasks,
 commit, LAUNCH BACKGROUNDED, checkpoint per task, ~75-min cap. MUST actually
 complete >=30 tasks this time.

Automated research step by research conductor.
